{"hits": {"hits": [{"metadata": {"citation_count": 67, "authors": [{"raw_affiliations": [{"value": "Microsoft Corporation, Redmond, WA, USA"}], "full_name_unicode_normalized": "simon, d.r.", "full_name": "Simon, D.R.", "record": {"$ref": "https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/2735095"}, "affiliations": [{"record": {"$ref": "https://inspirehep.net/api/institutions/905322"}, "value": "Microsoft, Redmond"}], "last_name": "Simon", "ids": [{"schema": "INSPIRE BAI", "value": "D.R.Simon.1"}], "first_name": "D.R.", "uuid": "e5acc9b4-1160-4afb-a59f-56763d38f335", "recid": 2735095}], "citation_count_without_self_citations": 67, "publication_info": [{"page_end": "123", "year": 1994, "page_start": "116"}], "$schema": "https://inspirehep.net/schemas/records/hep.json", "keywords": [{"source": "author", "value": "Quantum computing"}, {"source": "author", "value": "Turing machines"}, {"source": "author", "value": "Quantum mechanics"}, {"source": "author", "value": "Computational modeling"}, {"source": "author", "value": "Polynomials"}, {"source": "author", "value": "Computer simulation"}, {"source": "author", "value": "Physics computing"}, {"source": "author", "value": "Computer errors"}, {"source": "author", "value": "Lakes"}, {"source": "author", "value": "Relativistic quantum mechanics"}, {"source": "author", "value": "probabilistic automata"}, {"source": "author", "value": "computational complexity"}, {"source": "author", "value": "quantum computation"}, {"source": "author", "value": "quantum model of computation"}, {"source": "author", "value": "probabilistic model"}, {"source": "author", "value": "probabilistic Turing Machine"}, {"source": "author", "value": "complexity theory"}, {"source": "author", "value": "discrete logarithm"}, {"source": "author", "value": "integer factoring"}], "number_of_pages": 8, "inspire_categories": [{"term": "Quantum Physics"}], "author_count": 1, "first_author": {"full_name": "Simon, D.R.", "last_name": "Simon", "first_name": "D.R.", "recid": 2735095}, "control_number": 2735094, "dois": [{"source": "IEEE", "value": "10.1109/SFCS.1994.365701"}], "earliest_date": "1994", "document_type": ["conference paper"], "texkeys": ["Simon:1994ptx"], "abstracts": [{"source": "IEEE", "value": "The quantum model of computation is a probabilistic model, similar to the probabilistic Turing Machine, in which the laws of chance are those obeyed by particles on a quantum mechanical scale, rather than the rules familiar to us from the macroscopic world. We present here a problem of distinguishing between two fairly natural classes of function, which can provably be solved exponentially faster in the quantum model than in the classical probabilistic one, when the function is given as an oracle drawn equiprobably from the uniform distribution on either class. We thus offer compelling evidence that the quantum model may have significantly more complexity theoretic power than the probabilistic Turing Machine. In fact, drawing on this work, Shor (1994) has recently developed remarkable new quantum polynomial-time algorithms for the discrete logarithm and integer factoring problems.<<ETX xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">&gt;</ETX>", "abstract_source_suggest": {"input": "IEEE"}}], "titles": [{"source": "IEEE", "title": "On the power of quantum computation"}], "facet_author_name": ["2735095_D.R. Simon"], "core": true, "imprints": [{"date": "1994"}], "_oai": {"sets": ["Literature"], "id": "oai:inspirehep.net:2735094", "updated": "2024-09-17T09:32:41.921555"}, "curated": true}, "id": "2735094", "updated": "2024-09-17T09:32:41.921555+00:00", "created": "2023-12-12T06:40:14.610040+00:00", "links": {"bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2735094?format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2735094?format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2735094?format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2735094?format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2735094?format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2735094?format=cv", "citations": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A2735094"}}], "total": 1}, "links": {"self": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1109%2Fsfcs.1994.365701&size=5&page=1", "bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1109%2Fsfcs.1994.365701&size=5&page=1&format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1109%2Fsfcs.1994.365701&size=5&page=1&format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1109%2Fsfcs.1994.365701&size=5&page=1&format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1109%2Fsfcs.1994.365701&size=5&page=1&format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1109%2Fsfcs.1994.365701&size=5&page=1&format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=doi%3A10.1109%2Fsfcs.1994.365701&size=5&page=1&format=cv"}}